# ⚠️ AN ADS TEST BENCH, NOT A RELEASE. The file carries forciblySetPlatformId —
# it FORCES the SDK to pretend it is a platform. It is needed to run the live ads
# branch for the first time BEFORE uploading to the portal (otherwise the first
# execution in history of the code that brings money would happen on live
# players). But shipped into a release it would lie to the platform and to the
# players. Hence: committing it is impossible PHYSICALLY, not by agreement.
# How to use it — WORKSTREAMS, the INTEGRATION block.
playgama-bridge-config.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
Thumbs.db
*.pdf
3d assets/
avatars/_orig-p/
tools/lb-seed-bots.keys.json

# ⚠️ The itch.io hit-animations SOURCE pack (flashyfeather, hit-animations-vol2): 33 MB of
# 4096px sheets. The game embeds a REPACKED subset built by tools/hitfx-pack.py into
# src/app/37-hitfx.js — today eight effects at 192 px (the size and the list are the tool's
# arguments and have already changed twice; read the tool, not this line, for the live numbers).
# The raw pack must not enter the public repo — the licence covers use in a game, not the
# redistribution of the assets.
Hits2 Animations/

# ⚠️⚠️ THE BENCH ITSELF IS TRACKED — the owner asked for it to be kept («leave this document as an
# example of bonus-material variants, it will be useful again», 2026-09-01-l). Only its GENERATED
# self-contained copy is ignored, and that is not tidiness: `artifact.html` is written WITHOUT a
# doctype because the artifact host supplies the <head>, so served directly from GitHub Pages the
# same file falls into QUIRKS MODE and its WebGL viewports detach from the tiles they are scissored
# into (measured). Rebuild it with `python3 tools/variants-artifact.py` whenever it is needed.
electric-variants/artifact.html

# ⚠️ THE OWNER'S TWO INTRO MASTERS (2026-09-08): his 9:16 poster is inlined into the build as base64
# (the phone's splash) and his 10.2 MB HEVC video is what `video/blendo-intro.{webm,mp4}` were encoded
# from (ffmpeg, VP9 CRF 30 / H.264 CRF 19 — no browser but Safari decodes HEVC). The masters are his
# files at his paths — never re-encoded in place, never committed; the encodes in `video/` are tracked.
/Blendo-9-16-intro.jpg
/blendo-intro.mp4

# wrangler dev keeps its local state here (server/*/.wrangler)
.wrangler/

# `site/` is the folder the site Worker serves at blendo.monster — ASSEMBLED from the build by
# tools/site-pack.py (index.html, the bridge pair, music.mp3, avatars/), rebuilt on every build.py run and
# by `npm run site:deploy`. A product of the build, never a source (2026-09-09-c).
/site/
